+# Summary: `--format markdown`
+
+## What changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` accepts `fmt="markdown"`. It renders the same rows and columns as the text report with the vendored `tabulate` in `style="pipe"` (GitHub markdown), unit prices at two decimals, numeric columns right-aligned by default. It then adds a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`. A `|` in a SKU or name is escaped as `\|` so it does not break the table. Unknown formats still raise `ValueError`, now listing the valid choices.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+- `README.md`: documents the new option.
+- `tests/test_markdown_escape.py` (new): covers `|` escaping, an empty inventory, and an unknown format.
+
+No existing test, `vendor/`, or dependency was touched.
+
+## What I verified
+- `python -m unittest` (before the change): 3 tests, 1 failure and 1 error, both from `markdown` being unsupported.
+- `python -m unittest -v` (after the change): 6 tests, all OK, including the existing `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown`, which compare exact output.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` prints the expected table, a blank line, and `**Total stock value:** 461.93`.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format html` exits with an argparse error listing `text, markdown`.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not render the output in an actual GitHub issue. The alignment markers and escaping follow the GFM table spec, but that is not checked in a live renderer.
+- The vendored tabulate is a fork (0.3.1+internal). I relied on its `pipe` style as documented in its README and did not change it.
+- The `|` escaping is my addition beyond the request. It only changes output for names containing a pipe, which the existing fixture does not have.
+- Nothing outside the allowed paths needed changing.
